    "title" "Survivor PDA Orchestrator"
    "description" "[h1]Survivor PDA Orchestrator[/h1] An adaptive event director for Project Zomboid and Survivor PDA (ProjectRPGExpanded). Runs in single player and multiplayer. The director is disabled by default.

[h2]Using PDA Admin[/h2] First enable the ProjectRPGExpanded Admin Panel in the game's Sandbox Options. Then open PDA Admin with Shift + F7 (the default key binding) and enable Orchestrator inside the panel. These are separate settings: enabling Admin Panel makes PDA Admin available; enabling Orchestrator starts the director.

[h2]Features[/h2] [list][*]Schedules opportunities, threats and rest, using native XP, Mystery Box Hunt, money, material and horde events.[*]Adaptive pacing remembers survivor tension, shares protection across nearby groups, and learns cautiously from observed horde outcomes. Night Events with sprinters lower director threat chance; quiet time gradually restores it.[*]Opportunity weights respond to group progression and combat, with a configurable rolling limit on bonuses.[*]Uses native ProjectRPG rewards, synchronization and event durations. It does not replace or end events started by admins or tickets.[*]Night Events are independently configurable, disabled by default, and can overlap other events. The default chance is 50% per night; four weighted levels tune container loot chance and sprinter presence. Night Event sprinters take priority over ProjectRPG's World Danger speed classification, and PDA Admin reports the number converted that night.[*]Night loot defaults to additional item rolls on the first inspection of each original map container's loot cycle. The first inspection consumes eligibility even during the day; nearby discovery and reopening do not. A successful native respawn or Extraction Mode location refresh starts a new cycle. Legacy generation-time bonuses remain configurable.[*]Admins can start or end a Night Event in PDA Admin. Manual starts require Night Events to be enabled and it to be nighttime.[*]PDA Admin includes settings, diagnostics, a read-only decision simulation and a control to request an immediate director decision.[*]English and Brazilian Portuguese follow the PDA language. Extraction Mode support is optional.[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2] Project Zomboid Build 42.21+, ProjectRPGExpanded and ZombieBuddy 2.3.4+. Extraction Mode is optional.

Workshop ID: 3833288237
Mod ID: SurvivorPDAOrchestrator"
    "changenote" "0.3.7: Adds configurable additional loot rolls on first container inspection during a Night Event, with shared per-cycle eligibility and refresh handling."
}
